    example: 'If z_A·z_B is lower than z_A·z_other, the contrastive loss raises the positive similarity relative to the negative.',
    metrics: 'Report contrastive loss, retrieval alignment, and frozen linear-probe or downstream fine-tuning results. Low pretraining loss alone can hide collapsed or nontransferable representations.',
    whenNotToUse: 'Avoid transformations that erase task semantics, and avoid false negatives when distinct rows may represent the same underlying class or identity.',
    replacedBy: 'Negative-free objectives and masked prediction reduce dependence on very large negative sets; contrastive losses remain common in multimodal alignment.',
