    id: 'mae', name: 'Masked autoencoders', year: 2021, era: 'self-supervised', category: 'self-supervision', diagram: 'mae',
    source: { label: 'He et al., 2021', url: 'https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.06377' },
    whatItIs: 'A masked autoencoder removes a large subset of image patches, encodes only visible patches, and trains a lightweight decoder to reconstruct the missing pixels. It avoided the need to compare every example against negatives and made the encoder focus on contextual structure.',
    previousLimit: 'Contrastive learning depended strongly on paired augmentations, negative examples, and large effective batches.',
