    example: 'The decoder receives encoded visible patches plus learned mask tokens and predicts the RGB values at the 12 missing positions.',
    metrics: 'Use reconstruction loss for training health, but judge representation quality by linear probing or downstream fine-tuning. Sharp-looking reconstructions are not the objective and need not imply better features.',
    whenNotToUse: 'Do not use pixel reconstruction when the modality lacks local redundancy or when compute is too limited for a decoder and long token grid.',
    replacedBy: 'Representation-space prediction such as JEPA removes the requirement to reconstruct every pixel detail.',
