    source: { label: 'Hinton, Vinyals, and Dean, 2015', url: 'https://arxiv.org/abs/1503.02531' },
    whatItIs: 'Distillation trains a student to match a teacher’s softened output distribution, often alongside hard labels. It transfers relationships among classes or tokens that one-hot labels omit and can compress an expensive model into a cheaper one.',
    previousLimit: 'Training a small model only on hard labels discarded the richer behavior already learned by a large model.',
